          {
            "id": "2083615148611366996",
            "relation": "quote",
            "depth": 1,
            "sourceTweetId": "2083615148611366996",
            "author": {
              "name": "Andrew Curran",
              "handle": "AndrewCurran_",
              "avatarUrl": "https://pbs.twimg.com/profile_images/1596945208058744833/_X3LT7fb_normal.jpg",
              "isVerified": false
            },
            "content": "By the end of the year the tools available to anyone attempting this kind of attack will be vastly more capable across all devices. If there is a seam in any existing hardware, they will get their fingers in there. Attacks like this are about to start happening at scale.",
            "createdAt": "Sat Aug 01 18:05:37 +0000 2026",
            "viewCount": 115698,
            "metrics": {
              "views": 115698,
              "likes": 610,
              "retweets": 47,
              "replies": 49,
              "quotes": 5,
              "bookmarks": 108
            },
            "media": [],
            "translation": {
              "provider": "google",
              "status": "success",
              "language": "zh-CN",
              "text": "到今年年底，任何尝试此类攻击的人都可以使用的工具在所有设备上的功能都将大大增强。如果现有的硬件有缝隙，他们就会把手指伸进去。像这样的攻击即将开始大规模发生。",
              "annotations": [],
              "error": "",
              "updatedAt": "2026-08-03T00:05:06.117Z",
              "version": 1
            }
          },
          {
            "id": "2083527082223563157",
            "relation": "quote",
            "depth": 2,
            "sourceTweetId": "2083527082223563157",
            "author": {
              "name": "Jonathan Goodman 🇨🇦",
              "handle": "itscoachgoodman",
              "avatarUrl": "https://pbs.twimg.com/profile_images/1787182331062530048/p9BuedL4_normal.jpg",
              "isVerified": false
            },
            "content": "$1.6 million dollars in Bitcoin was drained from my account on July 29th in the Cold Card wallet hack.\n\nMy Bitcoin was in cold storage. My keys were on a ColdCard device kept in a safety deposit box that had never been connected to the internet.\n\nThis part's nerdy, but here's what happened:\n\nHackers discovered a vulnerability in the part of the hardware wallet code used to create seed phrases.\n\nThis allowed them to use AI to brute force guessing seed phrases.\n\nI was at our cottage and heard about the hack today.\n\n\"No way this affects me.\" I thought.\n\nI logged into Wasabi––software that lets me view my bitcoin wallets online.\n\nRight away I saw lines of red transaction–withdrawals–and I knew.\n\nFrom 9:36pm - 9:43pm on July 29th, every wallet I had had been emptied.\n\n18.25245043 btc gone. That's just over $1.6 million dollars CAD.\n\nPerhaps the hardest part about this is that I did everything right.\n\nI never shared my seed phrase with anybody. My devices never touched the internet. Everything was kept in multiple safes and safety deposit boxes.\n\nNone of it mattered. All because the hardware that created the seed phrase originally had one line in their code from 2021 that had a vulnerability.\n\nI'm filing a police report and a report with the Ontario Securities Commission. But I don't expect to recoup anything.\n\nA part of me is trying to make sense of what just happened. Or try to figure out a lesson in it. I'm struggling. $1.6 million is a staggering amount of money to have stolen.\n\nI guess all that I can think about right now is that I'm so damn happy that I'm an entrepreneur and that my earning potential is under my control. Mark my damn words. I'll recover.",
            "createdAt": "Sat Aug 01 12:15:41 +0000 2026",
            "viewCount": 7217347,
            "metrics": {
              "views": 7217347,
              "likes": 36676,
              "retweets": 3005,
              "replies": 4309,
              "quotes": 1282,
              "bookmarks": 7267
            },
            "media": [
              "https://pbs.twimg.com/media/HOosioZWwAAl_OZ.jpg"
            ],
            "translation": {
              "provider": "google",
              "status": "success",
              "language": "zh-CN",
              "text": "7 月 29 日，Cold Card 钱包遭到黑客攻击，160 万美元的比特币从我的账户中被盗走。\n\n我的比特币被冷藏。我的钥匙位于保管箱中的 ColdCard 设备上，该设备从未连接到互联网。\n\n这部分很书呆子气，但事情是这样的：\n\n黑客在用于创建助记词的硬件钱包代码部分中发现了一个漏洞。\n\n这使得他们能够使用人工智能来强力猜测种子短语。\n\n今天我在我们的小屋里听说了黑客事件。\n\n“这不会影响我。”我想。\n\n我登录了 Wasabi——一款可以让我在线查看我的比特币钱包的软件。\n\n我立刻看到了红色的交易线——取款——我就知道了。\n\n7月29日晚上9点36分到9点43分，我的钱包都被掏空了。\n\n18.25245043 BTC不见了。这刚刚超过 160 万加元。\n\n也许最困难的部分是我做的一切都是正确的。\n\n我从未与任何人分享过我的助记词。我的设备从未接触过互联网。所有东西都存放在多个保险箱和保险箱中。\n\n一切都不重要。一切都是因为创建助记词的硬件最初在 2021 年的代码中有一行存在漏洞。\n\n我正在向警方提交一份报告，并向安大略省证券委员会提交一份报告。但我不指望能收回任何东西。\n\n我的一部分正在试图理解刚刚发生的事情。或者尝试找出其中的教训。我正在挣扎。 160 万美元被盗的金额惊人。\n\n我想我现在能想到的就是我非常高兴我是一名企业家并且我的收入潜力在我的控制之下。记住我该死的话。我会康复的。",
              "annotations": [],
              "error": "",
              "updatedAt": "2026-08-03T00:05:06.811Z",
              "version": 1
            }
          }
        ],
